      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
